A timer line armed, or the watchdog fed, for a deadline nearer than any other of its core's leaves the core's timer where it was.
The timer would interrupt after the deadline and the thread sleep past it;
the nearest deadline a core's timer wakes for comes no later than that of any timer line armed there, or of the watchdog it fed.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: armed timer line comes due before the timer wakes for it
Report: the watchdog comes due before the timer wakes for it
Witness: fuzz cores-timer-across

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -41,7 +41,6 @@ static void wake_for(uint64_t deadline)
 {
     struct core *core = core_self();
     if (deadline < core->nearest_deadline) {
-        core->nearest_deadline = deadline;
         core->wake_stale = true;
     }
 }
